# 20 Newsgroups discriminative benchmark source audit v1

## Decision

Accept 20 Newsgroups for a local, non-redistributed CPU pilot.  The native
by-date split, native labels, sparse high-dimensional representation, and
metadata-leakage controls are sufficiently specified.  The original landing
page does not state an explicit corpus license; this is a publication and
redistribution limitation, not evidence of permission.  Raw posts and loader
caches therefore stay under `.deps/` and are excluded from checkpoints.

## Source findings

- The recovered maintainer page describes approximately 20,000 documents in
  20 native newsgroups.  Its recommended `20news-bydate` version contains
  18,846 documents, removes cross-post duplicates and several
  newsgroup-identifying headers, and uses a chronological 60% training / 40%
  test split.  The page explicitly recommends the split for deterministic
  cross-experiment comparison and temporal realism.
- The stable scikit-learn loader independently reports 20 classes and 18,846
  samples and exposes separate `train` and `test` subsets.
- Official documentation warns that headers, signatures, and quoted material
  can reveal the newsgroup.  The pilot therefore removes `headers`, `footers`,
  and `quotes` from both subsets.  Footers and quotes are heuristic filters and
  may be imperfect; this limitation survives any result.
- The official sparse example fits
  `TfidfVectorizer(sublinear_tf=True, max_df=0.5, min_df=5,
  stop_words="english")` on training text only and transforms test text with
  the fitted object.  The pilot freezes that feature construction.
- BSD markers on scikit-learn pages apply to documentation/example code.  No
  explicit license, permission, or copyright grant for the message corpus was
  located on the recovered maintainer page.  No dataset license is inferred.

## Leakage and evaluation contract

The native test labels are used only for final accuracy and macro-F1.  No test
document participates in vocabulary, IDF, SVD, subset selection, classifier
fit, hyperparameter selection, or stopping.  The metadata-removal policy is
fixed before download.  Dataset acquisition time is recorded separately; all
method-specific vectorization, subset/SVD construction, fitting, and prediction
times are counted.  Raw data are not checkpoint evidence; hashes, package
versions, dimensions, timings, metrics, and runner receipts are.

## Scope

This audit establishes benchmark admissibility only.  It does not establish
that a low-rank or coreset method helps a discriminative model and is not a
research cycle by itself.

